    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12360",
      "problem": "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $(-5) \\div (-3).$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we are dividing a negative number $({\\color{red}-5})$ by another negative number $({\\color{red}-3}).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152110/assets/28fcbc2c9986e631ed2310b8c90a917d87467be24e1b34dd3c4e87eec3650756.svg)\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n5 \\div 3 = 1 \\,\\textrm{R}\\, 2 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-5)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue} 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}}.\n$$",
